@startuml
title Delete the first chronological activity
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EDF3F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #526477
skinparam ArrowColor #526477
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "User" as User
participant "ui:Ui" as UI
participant "ConsoleHelper" as Console <<class>>
participant ":DeleteCommand" as Delete
participant "activities:ActivityList" as Activities

Console -> UI : readLine()
User -> UI : delete 1
UI --> Console : input

note over Console, Delete
  Parser has already created DeleteCommand(1).
end note
Console -> Delete : execute(activities, storage)
activate Delete
Delete -> Activities : deleteByDisplayedIndex(1)
activate Activities
Activities -> Activities : getByDisplayedIndex(1)
activate Activities
note right of Activities
  Read the canonical view.
  Check that the index exists.
  Select canonical.get(0).
end note
Activities --> Activities : removed
deactivate Activities
note right of Activities
  Remove that object from the backing list.
end note
Activities --> Delete : removed activity
deactivate Activities
Delete -> Activities : getActivities()
activate Activities
Activities --> Delete : insertion-order snapshot
deactivate Activities
note right of Delete
  Use the remaining size and removed
  activity's details in the message.
end note
Delete --> Console : result (didChangeActivities = true)
deactivate Delete
note over Console, Activities
  ConsoleHelper marks the change as unsaved,
  saves the updated activities, then displays
  the result. A failed save keeps the unsaved
  notice for a later bye retry.
end note
ref over User, Console
  CompletionAndSaveSequence
  result, activities, storage
end ref
@enduml
